          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "lakṣya is built on lakṣa, \"mark, sign, stake\", from the root √lakṣ, \"to mark, observe\" (MW). The Muṇḍaka Upaniṣad already uses it for an aim or target (CDIAL 10881). Lakṣa also became \"100,000\", the source of Hindi lākh."
            }
          ]
        },
